WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:03.040
Forget about fantastic beasts.

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:07.680
This time around, we're trying to find fantastic
reviews – and they're harder to come by

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:08.930
than you might think.

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:11.130
"Correct – three points to Hufflepuff."

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:16.480
"Fantastic Beasts: The Secrets of Dumbledore"
is the third film in the Wizarding World prequel

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:17.480
series.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:22.110
Directed by "Harry Potter" veteran David Yates,
it picks up several years after the events

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:26.420
of 2018's "Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes of
Grindelwald."

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:32.160
The new installment follows Professor Albus
Dumbledore as he enlists Magizoologist Newt

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:37.859
Scamander to help him fight against Gellert
Grindelwald, the dark wizard seeking out control

00:00:37.859 --> 00:00:38.899
of the wizarding world.

00:00:38.899 --> 00:00:39.899
J.K.

00:00:39.899 --> 00:00:44.699
Rowling, who wrote the first two films, returned
as a screenwriter, although this time she

00:00:44.699 --> 00:00:50.350
teamed up with Steve Kloves - aka the writer
of all but one of the "Harry Potter" films.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:55.840
The "Harry Potter" series is one of the most
successful franchises of all time, but the

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:00.690
"Fantastic Beasts" movie spin-offs haven't
quite seen the same success – with audiences

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:01.989
or critics.

00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:07.210
The first film in the prequel series, 2016's
"Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find Them,"

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:12.690
fared pretty well with its reviews, earning
itself a 74% score on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:18.140
However, the follow-up film, "Fantastic Beasts:
The Crimes of Grindelwald," didn't even come

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:23.420
close to achieving the same kind of success
with viewers — widely derided for its overstuffed

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:28.080
screenplay, it holds a Rotten Tomatoes rating
of just 36%.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:33.390
So, how does the upcoming "Secrets of Dumbledore"
compare to its predecessors when it comes

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:34.660
to critical consensus?

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:40.840
Well, as of the making of this video, it falls
squarely in the middle at a 62% score on the

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:41.930
Tomatometer.

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:45.000
Some reviews are okay with it – and some
really aren't.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.610
Here's a rundown of what these divided critics
think.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:50.820
"Things are not quite what they appear."

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:56.630
Despite "The Secrets of Dumbledore" nabbing
a better Tomatometer score than its 2018 predecessor,

00:01:56.630 --> 00:02:00.530
many critics were still not impressed with
the latest effort of the franchise.

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:04.740
Speaking for many of the critics who didn't
love the film, Entertainment Weekly declared

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:08.280
that "the third time is not quite the charm."

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:13.870
Some critics found that the film lacked focus,
and felt generally all over the place.

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:17.750
One of the critics, Kate Erbland of IndieWire,
wrote that the film offers

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:23.930
"...an unwieldy, mostly unsettling mash-up
of adult themes and childish whimsy, made

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:29.079
still more inscrutable by too many subplots,
too many characters, and a tone that veers

00:02:29.079 --> 00:02:31.879
wildly off-course at every possible turn."

00:02:31.879 --> 00:02:37.760
Meanwhile, Charles Bramesco of Polygon first
suggests the series should've called it quits

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:42.550
after the last movie before pointing out that
Newt — who began the series as the protagonist

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:47.129
— is barely involved in what's become the
actual plot of this series.

00:02:47.129 --> 00:02:48.359
He wrote,

00:02:48.359 --> 00:02:54.189
"Newt's convoluted, anticlimactic quest to
secure and deliver his precious cargo lacks

00:02:54.189 --> 00:02:59.280
the delighted curiosity that lent the first
'Fantastic Beasts' a much-needed bump in charm."

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:03.930
Finally, in a scathing review, Siddhant Adlakha
of IGN wrote,

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:09.109
"There are two more entries planned, but ending
the 'Harry Potter' spinoff here would be a

00:03:09.109 --> 00:03:10.109
mercy.

00:03:10.109 --> 00:03:12.020
There's nothing fantastic about the new movie.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:13.370
The story is dull.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:17.279
The characters are duller."

00:03:17.279 --> 00:03:18.959
"Ha!"

00:03:18.959 --> 00:03:20.349
It's not all bad, though.

00:03:20.349 --> 00:03:24.569
Though the review for Entertainment Weekly
implied the film missed the mark overall,

00:03:24.569 --> 00:03:28.180
writer Leah Greenblatt still found some merit
to the movie.

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:32.439
She concluded her review on the note that
"The Secrets of Dumbledore" is a major step

00:03:32.439 --> 00:03:37.450
up from its predecessor, deeming it, quote,
"nimbler and sweeter and more cohesive in

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:38.779
its storyline."

00:03:38.779 --> 00:03:43.459
Greenblatt also noted that this time around,
the cast are given more room to explore the

00:03:43.459 --> 00:03:48.529
stakes their characters face, instead of just
shuttling along from scene to scene.

00:03:48.529 --> 00:03:53.640
On the subject of the acting, Peter Debruge
of Variety noted that Mads Mikkelsen is better

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:57.999
suited for the character of Gellert Grindelwald
than Johnny Depp, who played the character

00:03:57.999 --> 00:03:59.730
in the previous film.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:05.939
Debruge wrote that Mikkelsen comes off favorably
as a "more grounded, less cartoonishly menacing"

00:04:05.939 --> 00:04:07.139
version of the character.

00:04:07.139 --> 00:04:11.999
He also gave credit to the screenplay, which
he found "far more focused" and "easier to

00:04:11.999 --> 00:04:13.720
follow" than the last one.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:18.709
In one of the most positive reviews — 4
out of 5 stars — Linda Marric of The Jewish

00:04:18.709 --> 00:04:24.160
Chronicle called it a "welcome return to form"
and gave special praise to the performances

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.820
of Law and Mikkelsen.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:27.280
She summed up the movie by saying,

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:31.870
"Yates, Rowling, and Kloves have given us
an engaging story peppered throughout with

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:35.230
some funny, heartfelt and exciting action
sequences."

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:37.370
What side of the divide will you be on?

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:42.310
The only way to find out is to see the movie
for yourself when "Fantastic Beasts: The Secrets

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:44.940
of Dumbledore" premieres in theaters on April
15.

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:47.360
"Who wouldn't like our chances?"

